  "question": {
    "text": "Two identical containers of the same emissivity contain liquid <math><mi>A</mi></math> and <math><mi>B</mi></math> at same initial temperature <math> <mrow> <mn>60</mn><msup> <mtext> </mtext> <mtext>o</mtext> </msup> <mtext>C</mtext></mrow> </math> and densities <math><msub><mrow><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub></math> &amp;<math><mi>&nbsp;</mi><msub><mrow><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mrow><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math> Which of the following plot best represents the temperature variation of both with time? (Given <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mn>J</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>k</mn><msup><mn>g</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mn>K</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> &amp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&nbsp;</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2000</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mn>J</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>k</mn><msup><mn>g</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mn>K</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>)",
